From: JeongBong Seo <lifeofthanks@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Share Mamba eviction pressure across cold paths

Keep the coverage-aware victim selector from 0008/0009 and put an
LRU-ordered, eviction-local round policy above it. Each non-branching
segment contributes one checkpoint per sweep while retaining two usable
device checkpoints. Count checkpoints with the existing match validators;
never refresh normal access recency to implement this second chance.

Repeat fair sweeps while they make progress. When no above-floor path can
contribute, restart at the true LRU tail and use the original hard-pressure
policy, so the soft floor cannot strand reclaimable slots. Preserve leaf
IO and session partition handling, and exclude load-back-pinned victims.

The exact-demand allocation backport and its v0.5.18 correction in 0010
are unchanged. The separate insertion-time maximum-state cap is unchanged;
a cap of two can leave every path already at this policy's soft floor.

---
